\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid 1 {\cf20 // dear imgui: Platform Backend for GLFW}\par
2 {\cf20 // This needs to be used along with a Renderer (e.g. OpenGL3, Vulkan, WebGPU..)}\par
3 {\cf20 // (Info: GLFW is a cross-platform general purpose library for handling windows, inputs, OpenGL/Vulkan graphics context creation, etc.)}\par
4 {\cf20 // (Requires: GLFW 3.1+. Prefer GLFW 3.3+ for full feature support.)}\par
5 \par
6 {\cf20 // Implemented features:}\par
7 {\cf20 //  [X] Platform: Clipboard support.}\par
8 {\cf20 //  [X] Platform: Mouse support. Can discriminate Mouse/TouchScreen/Pen (Windows only).}\par
9 {\cf20 //  [X] Platform: Keyboard support. Since 1.87 we are using the io.AddKeyEvent() function. Pass ImGuiKey values to all key functions e.g. ImGui::IsKeyPressed(ImGuiKey_Space). [Legacy GLFW_KEY_* values will also be supported unless IMGUI_DISABLE_OBSOLETE_KEYIO is set]}\par
10 {\cf20 //  [X] Platform: Gamepad support. Enable with 'io.ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad'.}\par
11 {\cf20 //  [X] Platform: Mouse cursor shape and visibility. Disable with 'io.ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_NoMouseCursorChange' (note: the resizing cursors requires GLFW 3.4+).}\par
12 {\cf20 //  [X] Platform: Multi-viewport support (multiple windows). Enable with 'io.ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_ViewportsEnable'.}\par
13 {\cf20 // Issues:}\par
14 {\cf20 //  [ ] Platform: Multi-viewport: ParentViewportID not honored, and so io.ConfigViewportsNoDefaultParent has no effect (minor).}\par
15 \par
16 {\cf20 // You can use unmodified imgui_impl_* files in your project. See examples/ folder for examples of using this.}\par
17 {\cf20 // Prefer including the entire imgui/ repository into your project (either as a copy or as a submodule), and only build the backends you need.}\par
18 {\cf20 // Learn about Dear ImGui:}\par
19 {\cf20 // - FAQ                  https://dearimgui.com/faq}\par
20 {\cf20 // - Getting Started      https://dearimgui.com/getting-started}\par
